      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think the option for world authors to upload a few extra screenshots would go a surprisingly long way on helping with this issue.\n\nAuthors of high effort worlds that want to attract visitors and ensure their world isn't missed, are quite likely to take a minute to include extra screen shots to show it off.\n\nAuthors of low effort or otherwise basic worlds that hope to trick users into visiting, will either be forced to show the actual world with those screenshots, or won't be able to provide any. If they choose to use additional fake images then that will generally be much easier to notice, and would highlight the deception as being fully deliberate. Worlds that refuse to upload any addition shots despite having an amazing looking thumbnail, would be less trusted and less viral as a result.\n\nJust this alone without even needing any ratings or active moderation, could likely solve the majority of the issue.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
